Third-party components

1) Build-time Rust crates. Husk is written in Rust; its dependencies are resolved
   by Cargo at build time and are not vendored here. Each crate keeps its own
   license; the build does not redistribute them.

2) One glibc artifact, used as a build input:

     tools/loader/ld-noble2404-ld.so   the unmodified dynamic loader from the
                                       Ubuntu 24.04 archive (`libc6`, arm64)

   glibc is licensed under the GNU Lesser General Public License v2.1 or later.
   It is redistributed unmodified solely so the loader can be rebuilt without a
   rootfs at hand; `docs/ENGINEERING.md` records its sha256. Corresponding
   source is available from the upstream GNU C Library and from the Ubuntu
   archive for the same version.

   Everything derived from it (`ld-embedded.so`, `libc-nop.so.6`,
   `libpath_shim.so`) is a build output: `make loader` produces it locally and it
   is not part of this source tree. Same for the App's own `jniLibs/*.so`, which
   `make apk` builds. None of these are covered by the Apache License 2.0 that
   applies to Husk's own source.

   A distribution release that only needs to run Husk does not require these
   files; see `docs/RUNNING.md`.

3) Brand assets under `docs/assets/brand/` are original artwork created for this
   project and are covered by the same license as the rest of the repository.

4) No part of the LinuxHub application, its private data, or its rootfs images is
   included in this repository.

5) FristOneRR PanVK 1.2.0 snapshot, redistributed in release bundles only when a
   Mali kbase device is present:

     vendor/panvk/fristonerr-1.2.0-mali-g77/

   Source: https://github.com/FristOneRR-Admin/FristOneRR-Panvk-Source
   Pinned source commit: 0c9dce35094dbe89c412b79bf57c6067c7b97e59
   Base: funnymdzz/mesa @ 6598829019c0746aa8e473b4ae1c980cbfa6ea4b
   License: MIT (Mesa and FristOneRR changes), with the original license text at
   the path above. `PROVENANCE.md` records the ELF Build ID, SHA-256 and the
   source patches applied by this project. This is a community build, not an
   official Mesa release and not an Adreno/Turnip driver.
